[Music]  millions of americans are spending  christmas in need  many suffering from the economic damage  of the pandemic  a texas singer who used to be homeless  is trying to offer cheer  and inspire others to help maria  villarreal shows us how this salvation  army bellringer  is using his voice for good  come and behold  the job is as recognizable as his voice  sammy wade is a bell ringer for the  salvation army's red kettle campaign on  the outskirts of fort worth texas  thing is he doesn't use that famous bell  he sings  across the walmart parking lot for all  to hear  all year has been a time when people  have been in need it was like that all  day  sammy would sing people like wendy lewis  would stop  stare in awe and give merry christmas  beautiful voice i walked out and i heard  this beautiful voice that stopped me  that one voice that one song stopped you  there are people that are hurting and  that are suffering  and the only thing that i can say is  that there is  hope he spent several years homeless the  one constant was his faith and since the  pandemic began  a new church helping him get back on his  feet  sammy has made such an impact on fellow  church members like david bell  that when his car broke down david  volunteered to drive him  i knew that if that job came through  i mean he had a ride that was just never  a question  that's 40 miles from here it's okay  [Music]  working on the red kettle campaign is a  full circle moment for the singer  who struggled after he was released from  prison for a nonviolent offense  three years ago sammy wade used to stay  at the salvation army  maybe social service center and we're  paying him but he's helping us  in return the red kettle campaign gave  sammy a temporary job for the holidays  he's working to get a new car and start  a voice coaching business  but more than anything he wants to help  restore people's faith and remind them  all is not lost i don't feel like crying  anymore  what makes you cry what part of this  i've said so many times  i'm not worthy of all this intention i'm  just someone who  just wants to just be like other people  no matter what  a hopeful soundtrack on a sidewalk in  the age of social distancing  for cbs this morning mireia villarreal  benbrook texas  what a beautiful story well done maria  and a powerful  powerful message there not just his  voice but his story  all of it coming full circle

